    "topic": "Digital Logic ",
    "front": "# 2020A_FE_AM_13\n\nECC is used for error detection and correction in memory. When n+2 redundant bits are required for a data bus having a width of 2n bits, what is the number of redundant bits that are required for a data bus having a width of 128 bits?\na) 3\nb) 8\nc) 9\nd) 10",
    "back": "c) 9\n### Step 1: Express 128 as a power of 2.\n\nData bits $= 128$\n$128 = 2^{7}$\n\n### Step 2: Apply the formula provided.\n\nNumber of redundant bits $= n + 2$\n$= 7 + 2 = 9$\n\n\n\n---"
